 ## Background
-This method is derived from basic ray-triangle intersection principles applied to the faces of an AABB [S1, S2, unofficial]. It is commonly found in educational graphics implementations and early-stage voxel engines where simplicity and explicit geometric handling are prioritized over raw performance [S1, S2, unofficial]. The specific implementation details, such as the use of `glm` vectors and the `AABBFaces` structure, are seen in the VoxelCore engine [S2, unofficial]. The approach is also referenced in academic projects like the CSE-333 Computer Graphics Volume Ray Casting project [S1, unofficial].
